{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/scripts/ensure-qualifier.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:06:52.354004Z","id":"b3e4db1d475cb25f4615eb830a42019768dc7024ec0843961f9daee66c420cc6","body":{"detail":"download_and_verify() (lines 186-209) verifies the tarball's sha256 before extracting, which is the stated defense against 'a tampered release' (line 50 comment). But is_pinned() (112-115), used by resolve_managed() (135-139) on every subsequent invocation, only checks that `$PLUGIN_HOME/$PINNED_VERSION/qualifier --version` prints the exact string `qualifier $PINNED_VERSION`. That string is fully controlled by whatever binary sits at that path -- a binary that got there by any means (a bug in a future edit to install_qualifier's rename/race handling, a local compromise, a stray write by another tool) satisfies the check trivially by hardcoding that one line of output. Once such a binary is in place, every future session (including the SessionStart hook, which runs it via bounded_summary) runs it without any further integrity check, since the checksum verification only ever runs on the download path.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":112},"end":{"line":139},"content_hash":"8b63c3824a4b965285a7d3e8722d9a682a68894e21b522387edabc513ab66b82"},"suggested_fix":"Either re-verify the managed install's own sha256 against the pinned checksum periodically (e.g. once per day, cached), or explicitly document in the header comment that the managed install is trusted for its lifetime based on version string alone and checksum verification applies only to fresh downloads, so a future reader doesn't assume the checksum protects the cached binary too.","summary":"A managed install, once cached, is trusted forever based only on its self-reported `--version` string, never re-checked against the pinned checksum","tags":["review","review:claude-plugin-pr14","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/scripts/ensure-qualifier.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:17:14.839393Z","id":"c8ab7d21cfe9f7b58c8eba316e318389b8dbd66ca30175ed273fef4c27534133","body":{"detail":"is_pinned() at plugins/claude-code/scripts/ensure-qualifier.sh:112-115 compares only the output of '\"$1\" --version' with 'qualifier $PINNED_VERSION'. resolve_managed() at :136-139 returns the managed path whenever is_pinned succeeds. sha256_of/expected_sha256 are called only in download_and_verify() at :186-209. The header (:14-15) does state the version-string check for step 2, but it never says that the checksum does not protect the cached binary. The comment at :50-51 ('so a tampered release is detected') can be read as covering it. The hook runs the resolved binary on every session start (plugins/claude-code/hooks/session-start:93,101 via bounded_summary).","kind":"comment","references":"b3e4db1d475cb25f4615eb830a42019768dc7024ec0843961f9daee66c420cc6","summary":"confirmed: a cached managed install is trusted from its --version output alone, and the checksum is checked only at download time","tags":["verified","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/scripts/ensure-qualifier.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T17:00:14.408466Z","id":"d53753489dbf4067006c44748521706f6062bd8afdedb073b7c7d4869586bee9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f475034bf27aef3af52166a50ed08a4a7f10904f","summary":"a cached install is now re-verified against its recorded sha256, not trusted on --version alone, and a stale hash forces reinstall: scripts/test-plugin.sh ok: a binary that does not match its recorded hash is reinstalled without being run; ok: a valid install with a matching hash record is reused without a download; also covered by commit fbcc098f02d433b20c9a6593156db0317909b2cf, verified by ok: an install made valid by a concurrent session before the set-aside is kept, not moved","supersedes":"b3e4db1d475cb25f4615eb830a42019768dc7024ec0843961f9daee66c420cc6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/scripts/ensure-qualifier.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:16:51.817624Z","id":"1ba6dccebc0597c57a48dfd270edfde8d628b4782908071cbd0dabcbd61f2e8e","body":{"detail":"release_target maps Linux-x86_64 to a static musl build (line 200) but Linux-aarch64 to aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu (line 201). On a musl aarch64 host (Alpine, or a common container base), the download and checksum pass, but the binary can't run. is_pinned then fails at lines 249-250 with \"the downloaded binary does not report qualifier 0.8.0\" and exits 1, without the cargo_fallback guidance. Nothing is installed, so every later call to the wrapper (each `exec`, and each SessionStart) downloads the tarball again. The hook then tells the user the download or checksum failed (session-start:127-129), which is not what happened.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":197},"end":{"line":204},"content_hash":"d45f47b1df66df1a86e9753656dbef760d7b83a4e2084af3cae177c82ae300dc"},"suggested_fix":"Publish an aarch64-unknown-linux-musl release and map Linux-aarch64 to it, as x86_64 already is. Or, when the downloaded binary fails to run, call cargo_fallback with a message that the prebuilt binary does not run on this system.","summary":"Linux aarch64 maps to a glibc build, so on a musl system it re-downloads on every call and reports a misleading error with no cargo fallback","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/scripts/ensure-qualifier.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:57.447049Z","id":"d15dc291e76d89399c2358b781551c8de45294b68431fcded6e08602a3440335","body":{"detail":"ensure-qualifier.sh:201 maps Linux-aarch64 to aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu. .github/workflows/release.yml:26-27 builds that target natively on ubuntu-24.04-arm without musl, so it is dynamically linked to glibc and can't exec on Alpine. is_pinned (ensure-qualifier.sh:125-127) then fails, and lines 249-250 log \"does not report qualifier\" and `exit 1` from staging, with no cargo_fallback and no install, so the next call downloads again. hooks/session-start:126-128 reports \"download or checksum failed\". Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"1ba6dccebc0597c57a48dfd270edfde8d628b4782908071cbd0dabcbd61f2e8e","summary":"confirmed: aarch64 Linux gets a glibc build, and a binary that won't run exits 1 without the cargo fallback","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
